<title>SWITZERLAND: UBS to cut about 800 domestic jobs.</title>
<headline>UBS to cut about 800 domestic jobs.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland said it will cut about 800 jobs as part of an extensive domestic restructuring.</p>
<p>&quot;The structural and organisational measures with which we intend to improve the efficiency of our operations will entail a reduction of 800 in our workforce in Switzerland,&quot; UBS chief executive Mathis Cabiallavetta said in the text of a speech released before a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;This reduction will be spread over the next two years,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>He did not make any reference to changes in job levels outside of Switzerland. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
